<%# Every icon, once per document, for <use> to reference.

    OPT-IN via config.x.icon_sprite, which Shared::UiHelper#icon reads to decide
    between <use> and inlining, and which the layout reads to decide whether to
    render this at all. It deliberately is NOT "has this partial run yet?" —
    Rails renders the template before the layout, so such a flag is set only
    after every content icon has already been emitted, and the page would inline
    its whole feed while the chrome below the sprite used it.

    Worth being concrete about why it is not simply on everywhere. The sprite is
    8.2KB flat. brgen's homepage draws 147 icons from 22 shapes and takes ~30KB
    off the document by it; amber draws 2 per page and bsdports draws 1, both
    only through shared partials, so switching them on cost bsdports 8.2KB
    against a 30KB page to save about 350 bytes. Measured before choosing.

    The whole set is emitted rather than only the icons a given page happens to
    call, because Turbo can inject markup after this renders — a turbo-stream
    appending a post carries <use href="#icon-repost"> and would draw nothing if
    the sprite had been trimmed to what the initial page needed.

    The paint attributes live on each <symbol>, not on the outer <svg> that
    Shared::UiHelper#icon emits, so they are written once instead of 147 times.
    That is safe here specifically because nothing overrides them: no stylesheet
    in the tree selects into icon output (the one `path`/`use` rule,
    _marketplace_animated_logo.scss's `.banner`, belongs to a self-contained logo
    partial that makes no icon() calls), and the helper exposes no paint
    argument. stroke="currentColor" still tracks the call site — currentColor
    resolves against the computed color inside the use shadow tree, which
    inherits from the element that referenced it.

    The inline style is deliberate and must not become `display:none` or
    `hidden`: a display:none sprite container stops <use> resolving in several
    engines, so the container has to stay rendered and be collapsed instead. Kept
    inline because it is a mechanical requirement of the technique rather than a
    visual decision. %>
<svg class="icon-sprite" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute"> <%# scan: intentional — width/height 0 must be inline or <use> stops resolving %>
  <% Shared::UiHelper::ICONS.each do |icon_name| %>
    <symbol id="icon-<%= icon_name %>" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><%= render "shared/icons/#{icon_name}" %></symbol>
  <% end %>
</svg>
